title    a mini, five by five
date     2026-07-29
tags     wasm puzzle play
stage    budding
wasm     crossword
---
Click the grid, then type. **Arrows** move, **tab** flips between across and
down, **?** checks what you have, **!** reveals the current letter.

The C owns the grid, the numbering and the answers. JavaScript draws a table
and forwards keystrokes — it never sees the solution, which is the only honest
way to ship a puzzle to a browser. **2KB** of wasm.

## the clues

:::
<div class="clueset">
<div><b>Across</b>
<ol class="clues">
<li value="1">Where the blood turns around</li>
<li value="6">What is left when the fire gives up</li>
<li value="7">Misuse, plainly</li>
<li value="8">Pine's slow blood; amber before it was amber</li>
<li value="9">The shape of a line, or the tyranny of one</li>
</ol></div>
<div><b>Down</b>
<ol class="clues">
<li value="1">The organ, or the courage</li>
<li value="2">A coal still thinking about it</li>
<li value="3">What a system does to the people inside it</li>
<li value="4">A violinist rubs it on the bow</li>
<li value="5">Statisticians love it; fashion needs it</li>
</ol></div>
</div>
:::

## the joke

The solution is a *symmetric word square*: reading down gives the same five
words as reading across. Across and down have different clues only so there is
something left to solve.

## numbering

Standard crossword numbering is computed in C, not hardcoded — a cell takes the
next number when nothing is filled to its left or above it. On a full square
that means the top row and the left column, which is why it runs 1–5 along the
top and 6–9 down the side. The rule generalises to grids with black squares
without a line changing.

See [[mandelbrot]] and [[garden-of-life]].
